  "body": "First part of issue 1456: the kernel-side reader for Solidcraft `.sc` designs. The app wiring is not in this PR (see \"Not in this PR\").\n\n## What changed\n- `camcraft_kernel::solidcraft::import_solidcraft(k, bytes, stop)` reads a `.sc` container and returns the cached **final body** as the same checked solidcore `StepSolid` the STEP reader hands out (mm, closed, positive volume), plus the design name, units and the writing app's version. It does not read parameters, sketches or feature history.\n- It reads only a cache that is provably this document's: `solidcraft-container/1`, document `solidcraft/<n>` in `mm`, cache format `solidcraft-model-cache/8` (the sample) or `/10` (the published source), producer `solidcraft-truck-adapter/4`, kernel `solidcore`, SHA-256 of `document.json` and of `cache/bodies.bin` both matching the manifest. The final state follows Solidcraft's own published rule (the last feature not skipped).\n- Refused by name: empty, not a ZIP, no end record, ZIP64, multi-disk, encrypted, a name listed twice, over 10,000 entries, an entry over its cap (container 4 KiB, manifest 32 MiB, parts 256 MiB), CRC-32 or length mismatch, a directory or data outside the file, an unknown method, an unknown container/document/cache version, another producer or kernel, inch (or any non-mm) units, no model cache, a **stale** cache (the document digest does not match), a payload digest mismatch, slices that overlap, leave gaps, run past or leave trailing data, a body run out of range, no evaluated feature, several bodies, a placed copy (assembly instance), a mesh body (`SCMESH01`), a bad magic, a body that does not decode. Entry names are only compared, never used as paths, and nothing is written to disk. A panic in the decoder or kernel is caught and reported; `stop` bounds the time.\n- New modules in `crates/kernel/src/solidcraft/`: `zip.rs` (a bounded in-memory ZIP directory reader written from APPNOTE.TXT), `sha256.rs` (FIPS 180-4, pinned by the standard's vectors), `cache.rs` (the manifest, slices and final state), `mod.rs`. `solidcore_step::build_record` is split out of the STEP reader's `build` so both share the same checks (no behaviour change for STEP).\n- Fixture: the maintainer's sample, `testdata/models/solidcraft_for_beginners.sc` (5 MB), marked binary in `.gitattributes`.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/1456-solidcraft-import.md`.\n\n## New dependency - needs the maintainer's yes\n`camcraft-kernel` gains `flate2 = \"1.1\"` (deflate for the container) and the workspace's `serde_json`. flate2 1.1.10 is **already in Cargo.lock** (png, tiff, usvg and vtkio pull it), so nothing new is downloaded or built; the lockfile gains two lines (the kernel's two new edges). The `zip` and `sha2` crates were considered and dropped (see the decision file). No new `camcraft-*` edge.\n\n## How tested\n- `crates/kernel/tests/solidcraft_import.rs` (Gate map: covers `camcraft_kernel::solidcraft`), 7 tests, all green in debug (~41 s):\n  - `sample_imports_its_final_body_at_the_design_size`: body \"Body1\", design name, mm, volume > 0, and the exact box equals the design's parameters (d1 = 125 mm diameter, d2 = 85 mm height): [-62.5, 62.5] x [-62.5, 62.5] x [0, 85] within 1e-6; the stored-ZIP rebuild of the same parts imports too.\n  - `not_a_container_is_refused`, `container_damage_is_refused`, `documents_we_cannot_read_are_refused`, `a_cache_that_is_not_this_documents_is_refused`, `a_bad_body_table_or_body_is_refused`: one corrupted copy per refusal above, built in the test, each asserting its message.\n  - `damaged_files_never_panic_or_hang`: 48 seeded byte-mutations/truncations of the sample plus 16 manifest-text mutations, under a 120 s cancel bound: no panic, no hang.\n- `solidcraft::sha256` unit test (FIPS vectors and padding edges).\n- Unchanged STEP suites re-run for the `build_record` split: `step_import`, `corrupt_input`, `machining_mesh` - green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick` falls back to the whole workspace for a `Cargo.toml` change and does not include camcraft-kernel; I ran the kernel suites above instead (the only crate touched).\n\n## Not in this PR / not exercised\n- **No app wiring**: Model > Open filter, drag-and-drop list and the MCP tool. No crate depends on `camcraft-kernel` yet (the app imports through truck until 917 lands); the first app -> kernel edge belongs there. So nothing is reachable from the GUI or MCP, and there was **no hand test in the app**.\n- **Finding, filed as 1463**: the machining mesh refuses this body at every chord tried (0.005-0.1 mm; deviation about 2.8x the tolerance). The refusal is the safe outcome, but the body cannot be machined until that is fixed, so the app wiring should wait for it or show that refusal.\n- Multi-body designs, assembly instances, mesh bodies, non-mm designs and cache formats other than 8 and 10 are refused, not read.\n- Release-mode and other OSes not run.\n\nChangelog: none (kernel-side reader only, not reachable from the app yet)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1456\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
